He, glory be to Him and exalted is He, mentions in this noble verse that He is the One who sends down to His servant Muhammad (ﷺ) ﴿clear signs﴾, meaning manifest ones. These are this Great Qur'an, so that through this Great Qur'an, which is described as ﴿clear signs﴾, He may bring people ﴿out of darknesses﴾, meaning out of the darkness of disbelief and sins, ﴿into light﴾, meaning the light of monotheism and guidance. The meaning contained in this noble verse is made explicit in His saying in Surat al-Talaq: ﴿So fear Allah, O you of understanding who believe. Allah has certainly sent down to you a reminder, a Messenger reciting to you the clear signs of Allah, that He may bring those who believe and do righteous deeds out of darknesses into light﴾ [al-Talaq: 10-11]. The verse of al-Talaq clarifies that the verse of al-Hadid belongs to what is called al-'amm al-makhsus (the general term that has been specified, i.e., a general expression restricted by a particular qualification), and that no one is brought out of darknesses into light by this Great Qur'an except those whom Allah has enabled to believe and to do righteous deeds. So His saying in al-Hadid, ﴿that He may bring you out of darknesses﴾ [al-Hadid: 9], means, on the condition of faith and righteous deeds, as evidenced by His saying: ﴿that He may bring those who believe and do righteous deeds out of darknesses﴾ [al-Talaq: 11], and so on.

The call to believe in the Qur'an and to be brought out by its light from the darkness of disbelief is general, but the enabling to be brought out by it from darknesses into light is specific to those whom Allah has enabled, as the cited verses of al-Talaq indicate. Allah, glory be to Him and exalted is He, says: ﴿And Allah invites to the Abode of Peace and guides whom He wills to a straight path﴾ [Yunus: 25].

What this noble verse contains, namely that the Qur'an is a light by which Allah brings the believers out of darknesses into light, is also explained in verses of the Book of Allah:

• such as His saying, exalted is He: ﴿O mankind, there has certainly come to you a proof from your Lord, and We have sent down to you a manifest light﴾ [al-Nisa': 174];

• and His saying: ﴿There has certainly come to you from Allah a light and a clear Book, by which Allah guides whoever follows His pleasure to the ways of peace and brings them out of darknesses into light by His permission and guides them to a straight path﴾ [al-Ma'idah: 15-16];

• and His saying: ﴿So believe in Allah and His Messenger and the light which We have sent down﴾ [al-Taghabun: 8];

• and His saying: ﴿So those who believed in him, honored him, supported him, and followed the light that was sent down with him — it is those who are the successful﴾ [al-A'raf: 157];

• and His saying: ﴿But We made it a light by which We guide whom We will of Our servants﴾ [al-Shura: 52], and the verse that follows it.
